@startuml qnx_dispatch_server_read_activity
title QnxDispatchServer - native read and queue retirement

start
:Enter ProcessReadRequest(ctp) from native server request dispatch;
:Lock send_mutex_;
if (send_queue_ is empty?) then (yes)
    :Unlock and return EAGAIN;
    stop
else (queued record)
    :Reference the front record without removing it;
endif
:Build two I/O vectors for the code byte and payload;
:Compute header size + payload size\nCast to int32_t for _IO_SET_READ_NBYTES;
:Recover server and call MsgReplyv(ctp->rcvid, ctp->status, vectors)\nIgnore its result;
:Pop the record from send_queue_;
if (Record code is NOTIFY?) then (yes)
    :Push the record back to notify_pool_;
else (REPLY)
    :Leave the embedded reply record outside both lists;
endif
:Unlock and return _RESMGR_NOREPLY;
stop

legend
    The mutex covers the native reply attempt and record retirement.
    A record is consumed even if MsgReplyv fails; no retry is queued here.
    This method adds no requested-read-size or int32_t-range guard.
    HasSomethingToRead separately locks and tests whether the FIFO is non-empty.
endlegend

@enduml
